Example: a cash deposit is a contribution, not investment profit.
The only selected holding is Assets:Cash in USD. The journal adds 100 USD on
2024-01-01, so the closing value and net contributions are both 100 USD.
Profit/loss is ending value 100 minus opening value 0 minus contributions 100 = 0.
The daily value equals the contribution, so the time-weighted return is 0.
The money-weighted fields are null: all investor cash flows fall on one date,
which supplies no elapsed time for an annualized return.

========== API ==========

investmentPerformance({ accounts: ['Assets:Cash'], commodities: ['USD'], from: '2024-01-01', to: '2024-01-01' })

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
account Assets:Cash
account Equity:Opening

2024-01-01 Deposit
  Assets:Cash  100 USD
  Equity:Opening  -100 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

{
  "from": "2024-01-01",
  "to": "2024-01-01",
  "commodities": [
    "USD"
  ],
  "valuationCommodity": "USD",
  "openingValue": 0,
  "endingValue": 100,
  "netContributions": 100,
  "profitLoss": 0,
  "timeWeightedReturn": 0,
  "moneyWeightedReturn": null,
  "moneyWeightedReturnTotal": null,
  "points": [
    {
      "date": "2024-01-01",
      "value": 100,
      "netContributions": 100,
      "profitLoss": 0,
      "timeWeightedReturn": 0,
      "moneyWeightedReturn": null,
      "moneyWeightedReturnTotal": null
    }
  ]
}

========== WARNINGS ==========
